# THE HUSH (docs/HUSH.md H3): in a crags ring the world falls silent -- every
# bed and scatter sound gone (`await beds_silent`, 70_audio), the player's own
# left -- and the air holds: the grass and the fog stop moving. Proven by the
# frames: two half a second apart in the quiet differ no more than two half a
# second apart once it lifts, over the right of the frame (the sea on the
# left moves by its own clock, as it should). `--hush=always` makes every visit answer, so the
# proof does not wait on a night's hash; fog by day, so the grass is seen.
# From above, then out and back in over the shoulder.
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/hush-quiet.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=fog:0.6:wind=0.9 --hush=always
place the_crags
coast calm
wait 1.0
near hush_ring
await hush_quiet 6
await beds_silent 4
shot 01-silent-a
wait 0.5
shot 02-silent-b
await hush_gone 15
wait 1.0
shot 03-moving-a
wait 0.5
shot 04-moving-b
same 01-silent-a 02-silent-b no_more_than 03-moving-a 04-moving-b 1900,252,1900,1700
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
walk 0,1 2.0
wait 0.5
near hush_ring
await hush_quiet 6
shot 05-silent-over-the-shoulder-a with shoulder
wait 0.5
shot 06-silent-over-the-shoulder-b with shoulder
await hush_gone 15
wait 1.0
shot 07-moving-over-the-shoulder-a with shoulder
wait 0.5
shot 08-moving-over-the-shoulder-b with shoulder
same 05-silent-over-the-shoulder-a 06-silent-over-the-shoulder-b no_more_than 07-moving-over-the-shoulder-a 08-moving-over-the-shoulder-b 1900,252,1900,1700
